{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionColourActionBaseModule","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.OctonionComplexStructure","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Determinant","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Lemmas"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.Le_neg_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.Le_neg_ne","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L127-L137","doc":"The two complex structures are different. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.negLe_commutes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.negLe_commutes","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L122-L125","doc":"Every element of the stabilizer of `e₁` commutes with `−L_{e₁}` as well as with `L_{e₁}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.negLe_sq_eq_neg_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.negLe_sq_eq_neg_id","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L118-L120","doc":"`−L_e` is also a complex structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.octMulₗ_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.octMulₗ_neg","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L114-L116","doc":"Left multiplication by `−e` is `−L_e`: the second complex structure is `L_{−e}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.su3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.su3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L109-L112","doc":"**`su3 (−e) = su3 e`**: a derivation kills `−e` iff it kills `e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.tower_triplet_no_complex_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.tower_triplet_no_complex_structure","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L102-L105","doc":"The tower's colour triplet `ℚ³` carries no complex structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.no_complex_structure_of_odd_finrank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.no_complex_structure_of_odd_finrank","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**No complex structure on an odd-dimensional space** over a linearly ordered field:\n`det(J)² = det(J ∘ J) = det(−1) = (−1)^{dim} = −1` is impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.colourStabilizerAction_on_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.colourStabilizerAction_on_three","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L78-L84","doc":"The tower's colour triplet `ℚ³` already satisfies the class for any 8-dimensional colour\nalgebra, with no reference to octonions or to the Hecke structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.colourStabilizerAction_of_finrank_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.ColourBridgeObstructions.colourStabilizerAction_of_finrank_le","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/ColourBridgeObstructions.lean#L55-L76","doc":"**Any `g` with `finrank g ≤ (finrank V)²` acts faithfully on `V`**, by a map built from bases\nonly. Together with `not_colourStabilizerAction_of_dim_sq_lt` this makes\n`ColourStabilizerAction g V` equivalent to `finrank g ≤ (finrank V)²`: the class records a\ndimension count, not a bridge. ","signatureChunk":0}]}